{"ClientSettings":{"Pn":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"P"},"Sc":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"H"},"Qz":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"T"},"Ap":true,"Mute":true,"Lad":"2026-08-30T00:00:00Z","Iotd":0,"Gwb":0,"Tns":0,"Dft":null,"Mvs":0,"Flt":0,"Imp":1,"Tobn":0},"MediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"From the cliffs of Lloret de Mar in Girona, Catalonia, the Camí de Ronda winds along the Costa Brava, a coastline true to its name: wild, rugged and full of surprises. This historic route passes hidden coves, rocky outcrops battered by the Mediterranean and pine forests that reach almost to the sea. It was originally established so that customs officers could patrol the coastline and help prevent smuggling. Today, it is considered one of the most spectacular coastal walks in Spain.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.LloretdeMar_ROW9048268267_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.LloretdeMar_ROW9048268267_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Camí de Ronda, Lloret de Mar, Catalonia, Spain","Copyright":"© MEDITERRANEAN/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260829_LloretdeMar\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Cami+de+Ronda&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260829_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260829_LloretdeMar"},"Ssd":"20260829","Name":"LloretdeMar","Market":"ROW","Hash":"9048268267","FullDateString":"29 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"At sunset, Mont-Saint Michel rises from the waters of Normandy, France, like a fortress shaped by the sea. Perched on a rocky tidal island, the abbey and village stand at the centre of one of Europe's most dramatic coastal settings. Twice a day, the sea retreats to reveal vast stretches of sand before surging back to reclaim the landscape. At high tide, the mount becomes an island once again. For centuries, travellers timed their journeys to this rhythm, crossing the flats when conditions allowed and watching the sea return hours later.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.MichelSunset_ROW7306712328_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.MichelSunset_ROW7306712328_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Mont-Saint-Michel during high tide, Manche, Normandy, France","Copyright":"© Clement LEONARD/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260828_MichelSunset\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Mont+Saint+Michel&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260828_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260828_MichelSunset"},"Ssd":"20260828","Name":"MichelSunset","Market":"ROW","Hash":"7306712328","FullDateString":"28 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Imagine a world without the natural wonders that hold about 90% of Earth's surface freshwater. Lakes are among our planet's most valuable resources. More than 117 million lakes cover nearly 4% of Earth's land surface, yet many face growing pressure from pollution, overuse and climate change.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.LakeMagadi_ROW6887242207_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.LakeMagadi_ROW6887242207_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Lesser flamingo flock at sunrise, Lake Magadi, Kenya","Copyright":"© Denis-Huot/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260827_LakeMagadi\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Lesser+flamingo&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260827_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260827_LakeMagadi"},"Ssd":"20260827","Name":"LakeMagadi","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6887242207","FullDateString":"27 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"As darker nights return to Iceland, visitors will soon look to the skies for a chance to see the aurora borealis. Better known as the northern lights, this luminous phenomenon occurs when particles from the sun interact with gases high in Earth's atmosphere, creating shimmering ribbons of green, pink, purple and sometimes red light. Iceland's northern location and increasingly dark autumn and winter nights make it one of the world's premier destinations for aurora viewing.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AurorasIceland_ROW6294379114_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AurorasIceland_ROW6294379114_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Auroras over Kirkjufell, Iceland","Copyright":"© Cavan Images/Alamy","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260826_AurorasIceland\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Aurora+borealis&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260826_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260826_AurorasIceland"},"Ssd":"20260826","Name":"AurorasIceland","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6294379114","FullDateString":"26 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"The walk begins with a patch of sunlight on the trail, then the redwoods seem to close around the path. Today's image from Redwood National and State Parks in California, USA, shows the scene many visitors remember most: towering trunks, ferns underfoot and moss clinging to fallen wood. The parks take their name from the coast redwood, Sequoia sempervirens, whose thick, reddish bark helps protect it from fire. After decades of extensive logging, Redwood National Park was created in 1968 and later expanded in 1978 to strengthen protection for old-growth forests.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.RedwoodPark_ROW5740708229_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.RedwoodPark_ROW5740708229_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Sunrise in Redwood National and State Parks, California, United States","Copyright":"© HadelProductions/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260825_RedwoodPark\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Redwood+National+and+State+Parks&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260825_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260825_RedwoodPark"},"Ssd":"20260825","Name":"RedwoodPark","Market":"ROW","Hash":"5740708229","FullDateString":"25 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"The Brooklyn Bridge doesn't just connect Manhattan and Brooklyn—it bridges history, engineering and a few surprising stories too. Opened in 1883 after 14 years of construction, it became the world's first steel-wire suspension bridge, forever changing the way New Yorkers crossed the East River.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.BKBridge_ROW5406513289_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.BKBridge_ROW5406513289_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Brooklyn Bridge, New York City, United States","Copyright":"© shayes17/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260824_BKBridge\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Brooklyn+Bridge&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260824_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260824_BKBridge"},"Ssd":"20260824","Name":"BKBridge","Market":"ROW","Hash":"5406513289","FullDateString":"24 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"In Alaska, some of the world's wildest wildlife spectacles unfold far from cities and roads. At Katmai National Park, brown bears line the river, and when the salmon jump, the show begins. Created in 1918 after the dramatic 1912 Novarupta volcanic eruption, the park protects more than 16,000 square kilometres of wilderness, including active volcanoes, tundra and salmon-rich rivers.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.KatmaiBear_ROW4890016899_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.KatmaiBear_ROW4890016899_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Brown bear fishing in river, Katmai National Park, Alaska, United States","Copyright":"© Pal Hermansen/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260823_KatmaiBear\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Katmai+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260823_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260823_KatmaiBear"},"Ssd":"20260823","Name":"KatmaiBear","Market":"ROW","Hash":"4890016899","FullDateString":"23 Aug 2026"}],"PreloadMediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"When it comes to aerial acrobatics, hummingbirds are in a league of their own. Found only in the Americas, these tiny birds can hover in place, fly backwards and beat their wings dozens of times per second. As they visit flowers in search of nectar, they also serve as important pollinators, helping sustain ecosystems from alpine meadows to tropical rainforests. Their shimmering plumage, remarkable agility and high-energy lifestyles make them some of the world's most fascinating birds.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.GreenCrowned_ROW0730008155_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.GreenCrowned_ROW0730008155_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Green-crowned brilliant hummingbirds feeding on lobster-claw flowers, Costa Rica","Copyright":"© Paul Hobson/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260905_GreenCrowned\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Green-crowned+brilliant&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260905_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260905_GreenCrowned"},"Ssd":"20260905","Name":"GreenCrowned","Market":"ROW","Hash":"0730008155","FullDateString":"5 Sept 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Rising above the salt marshes along Germany's North Sea coast, the Westerheversand Lighthouse is instantly recognisable thanks to its distinctive red-and-white stripes. Built between 1906 and 1908, the lighthouse has stood as an icon on the Eiderstedt Peninsula for more than a century, guiding ships through the waters of the North Sea. Today, it remains one of northern Germany's best-known coastal landmarks. Visitors who climb its 157 steps are rewarded with sweeping views of the surrounding scenery.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.Westerheversand_ROW0428047340_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.Westerheversand_ROW0428047340_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Westerheversand Lighthouse in Westerhever, Schleswig-Holstein, Germany","Copyright":"© bluejayphoto/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260904_Westerheversand\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Westerheversand+Lighthouse&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260904_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260904_Westerheversand"},"Ssd":"20260904","Name":"Westerheversand","Market":"ROW","Hash":"0428047340","FullDateString":"4 Sept 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Blink and you'll miss the turn, but you definitely won't miss the cliffs. Vermilion Cliffs National Monument stretches across northern Arizona and protects a landscape shaped over nearly 200 million years. The area became a national monument in 2000, helping safeguard fragile rock formations, prehistoric sites and habitats for rare wildlife. Coyote Buttes is the star attraction for many visitors. Its famous Wave is carved into Navajo Sandstone, which began as vast sand dunes during the Jurassic Period. Over millions of years, wind erosion, rainfall and temperature changes sculpted the flowing bands and curves seen today.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AZWilderness_ROW6879233352_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AZWilderness_ROW6879233352_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Coyote Buttes, Vermilion Cliffs National Monument, Arizona, United States","Copyright":"© James Hager/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260903_AZWilderness\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Vermilion+Cliffs+National+Monument&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260903_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260903_AZWilderness"},"Ssd":"20260903","Name":"AZWilderness","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6879233352","FullDateString":"3 Sept 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Along England's east shore, the Suffolk Heritage Coast blends windswept heaths, marshes, shingle beaches and expansive North Sea views. One of its best-known towns is Southwold, where water and history are inseparable. Almost encircled by the sea, the River Blyth and surrounding wetlands, the town occupies a slender peninsula shaped by centuries of fishing, trade and life at the edge of the water.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SuffolkHuts_ROW5530395883_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SuffolkHuts_ROW5530395883_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Traditional beach huts, Southwold, Suffolk Heritage Coast, England","Copyright":"© stevendocwra/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260902_SuffolkHuts\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Southwold+Suffolk&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260902_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260902_SuffolkHuts"},"Ssd":"20260902","Name":"SuffolkHuts","Market":"ROW","Hash":"5530395883","FullDateString":"2 Sept 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Fungi often go unnoticed beneath forest floors, lawns and fallen leaves, yet their underground threads help recycle nutrients and support healthy ecosystems. The mushrooms we see are only the fruiting bodies of much larger organisms. They appear briefly, release spores, then disappear from sight. Unlike plants, fungi belong to a kingdom of their own. Some species even glow, while others form partnerships with trees.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.HorseHairShroom_ROW4884226471_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.HorseHairShroom_ROW4884226471_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Horsehair parachute fungus, Belarus","Copyright":"© Máté/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260901_HorseHairShroom\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Fungus&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260901_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260901_HorseHairShroom"},"Ssd":"20260901","Name":"HorseHairShroom","Market":"ROW","Hash":"4884226471","FullDateString":"1 Sept 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"When the first rays of sunlight gild the horizon, Sellin Pier reveals its most striking side. Located on the eastern coast of the island of Rügen in Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania, this structure is one of the best-known landmarks on Germany's Baltic coast. Its history dates back to 1906, when the first pier was opened. Over the decades, the structure suffered repeated damage from storms and other factors and was eventually demolished.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SellinSunrise_ROW9214234977_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SellinSunrise_ROW9214234977_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Sellin Pier, Rügen, Germany","Copyright":"© bluejayphoto/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260831_SellinSunrise\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Sellin+Pier&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260831_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260831_SellinSunrise"},"Ssd":"20260831","Name":"SellinSunrise","Market":"ROW","Hash":"9214234977","FullDateString":"31 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Imagine coming face to face with a fish the size of a bus. The whale shark is the world's largest fish, yet it is a remarkably gentle giant. Despite its name, it is not a whale but a shark, with the biggest confirmed individuals measuring around 18 metres long and weighing more than 20 tonnes. Found in warm tropical and subtropical seas, whale sharks move slowly through the water with their mouths open, filtering plankton, fish eggs and other tiny prey. Their distinctive white spots and stripes form patterns unique to each individual, allowing researchers to identify and track them over time.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.YellowShark_ROW3439446140_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.YellowShark_ROW3439446140_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Whale shark and golden trevally, Cenderawasih Bay, West Papua, Indonesia","Copyright":"© Pete Oxford/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260830_YellowShark\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Whale+shark&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260830_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260830_YellowShark"},"Ssd":"20260830","Name":"YellowShark","Market":"ROW","Hash":"3439446140","FullDateString":"30 Aug 2026"}],"LocStrings":{"LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_IOTD":"Image of the day","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_IOTD_LEARN_MORE":"Learn more","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_DONATE_NOW":"Donate now","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_FACT":"Quick fact:","LOC_HOMEPAGE_GALLERY_CARD_TITLE":"Recent Homepage images","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_GALLERY_IMAGE_ARIALABEL":"Homepage image for {0}","LOC_HOMEPAGE_ON_THIS_DAY_TITLE":"On this day in history","LOC_HOMEPAGE_ON_THIS_DAY_IMAGE_ARIALABEL":"On this day in {0}, {1}","LOC_HOMEPAGE_SHARE_TOOLTIP":"Share today's Bing homepage","LOC_HOMEPAGE_WALLPAPERDOWNLOAD_TOOLTIP":"Download this image. Use of this image is restricted to wallpaper only.","LOC_MUSCARD_DOWNLOAD_LINK":"Download this image","LOC_HOMEPAGE_WALLPAPERNOTAVAILABLE":"This image is not available to download as wallpaper.","LOC_HOMEPAGE_INFO_TEXT":"Info","LOC_BING_WP_APP_LINK":"https://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/?linkid=2127455","LOC_BING_WP_APP_LINK_TEXT":"Get the Bing Wallpaper app","LOC_BING_APP_TEXT":"Get Bing Wallpaper on your devices","LOC_BING_APP_LINK_PC":"https://bing.microsoftapp.net/bing/?adjust=nk9xri2_dzfz5n2","LOC_BING_APP_LINK_MOBILE":"https://app.adjust.com/d93ddtl_a75k0gg?deeplink=sapphire%3A%2F%2Fwallpaper","LOC_BING_APP_DOWNLOAD_TEXT":"Mobile App","LOC_BING_WP_APP_DOWNLOAD_TEXT":"Desktop App","LOC_BING_APP_TEXT_MOBILE":"Get daily photos with Bing App","LOC_BING_APP_DOWNLOAD_TEXT_MOBILE":